;
LDIR - LIST THE MEMBERS OF A LIBRARY

CALLER. Subject to current caller access policy.

A - List the members of a library

:A
LIST THE MEMBERS OF A LIBRARY

    LDIR DU:library
    LDIR NAME:library

LDIR-B 1.5 examines an LBR library without extracting its members.
For example, on the default P: archive:

    LDIR P0:SIGMV011
    LDIR SIGM:SIGMV011

Use the member names in the listing when reading documentation with LT.

    LT P0:SIGMV011 ABSTRACT.011

Supply the actual member name shown by LDIR. Some members are compressed.
LDIR does not unpack them into WORK or execute programs in the library.
To take the whole library home, use YSEND with its .LBR filename.

See HELP LT, HELP LIBRARY and HELP YSEND.
